# Question 1
- Read the file `data/gene_expression.csv` into a DataFrame called `df`. Display the first 5 rows of the DataFrame.
<br></br>

# Question 2
- Filter the DataFrame `df` to only include rows where the '**Fold_Change**' column is greater than 2. Write the filtered DataFrame to a new CSV file named `output/upregulated_genes.csv`.

(We have not yet covered filtering rows with Pandas but try using the following hint to help).

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: To filter rows, use the following syntax:

`filtered_df = df[df['Column_Name'] > value]`
<br></br>


# Question 3
- Read the TSV file `data/patient_data.tsv` into a DataFrame. Calculate the average age of the patients and print the result.

(We have not yet covered calculating column averages with Pandas but try using the following hint to help).

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: To calculate the mean average of a column, use the following syntax:

`column_mean = df['Column_Name'].mean()`
<br></br>

